From f7898ca524181c5e0f76b0cab49c2e55c6bd2218 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TofuJoe <darryl.hon@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:26:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] drm/xe: Refresh LRU position of long-running VMs on
 exec

For VMs in dma-fence mode, exec moves the VM private BOs to the LRU tail on
every submission. Long-running (preempt-fence) VMs skipped that and were only
refreshed by the rebind worker, so a VM that keeps submitting drifts towards
the LRU head and is evicted first under memory pressure, suspending its
queues only for the rebind worker to swap it straight back in.

Do the same O(1) bulk move for LR VMs, guarded by a trylock of the VM resv
(which covers every BO in the bulk range).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_exec.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_exec.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_exec.c
index 70db369..7a9e4cc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_exec.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_exec.c
@@ -360,6 +360,20 @@ retry:
 		spin_lock(&xe->ttm.lru_lock);
 		ttm_lru_bulk_move_tail(&vm->lru_bulk_move);
 		spin_unlock(&xe->ttm.lru_lock);
+	} else if (!err && dma_resv_trylock(xe_vm_resv(vm))) {
+		/*
+		 * Long-running VMs don't lock their BOs on exec, so their LRU
+		 * position was only refreshed by the rebind worker. A VM that
+		 * keeps submitting then drifts to the LRU head and is the first
+		 * thing the shrinker evicts, which suspends its queues and
+		 * rebinds them right back. The bulk range only holds BOs that
+		 * share the VM resv, so holding it is enough; skip the refresh
+		 * if someone else holds it (e.g. an eviction or rebind).
+		 */
+		spin_lock(&xe->ttm.lru_lock);
+		ttm_lru_bulk_move_tail(&vm->lru_bulk_move);
+		spin_unlock(&xe->ttm.lru_lock);
+		dma_resv_unlock(xe_vm_resv(vm));
 	}
 
 	if (mode == EXEC_MODE_LR)
-- 
